{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 3, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**Summary of the Wikipedia page \"Raymond III Count of Tripoli\"**\n\nRaymond III was Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II of Tripoli and Hodierna of Rethel. Raymond III became count at a young age after his father was assassinated in 1152. His mother Hodierna and grandfather Count Joscelin II of Edessa ruled Tripoli as regents until he came of age. Raymond III was raised in the Principality of Antioch and later returned to Tripoli to assume power.\n\n*highlighted section part 1*\n\nRaymond III played a significant role in the politics of the Crusader states. He was a key ally of Bohemond III of Antioch and Amalric I of Jerusalem. In 1164 he was captured by Nur ad-Din at the Battle of Harim and held prisoner for nearly ten years. During his captivity Tripoli was ruled by his cousin Aimery of Lusignan. Raymond III was released in 1173 after a ransom was paid. Upon his return he resumed control of Tripoli and continued to be a major figure in the region.\n\n*highlighted section part 2*\n\nIn 1174 Raymond III supported the succession of Baldwin IV the Leper as King of Jerusalem. He opposed the influence of Miles of Plancy and later Raymond of Tripoli’s role in the regency for Baldwin IV’s half-sister Sibylla. In 1177 he commanded the vanguard at the Battle of Montgisard where Baldwin IV defeated Saladin. Raymond III was also involved in the succession crisis following Baldwin IV’s death in 1185. He supported Humphrey IV of Toron against Guy of Lusignan but ultimately Humphrey married Isabella of Jerusalem which complicated the matter.\n\n*highlighted section part 3*\n\nRaymond III died in 1187 without a male heir. His death marked the end of the original Counts of Tripoli from the House of Poitiers. His territory passed to his cousin Raymond IV of Toulouse who became Count of Tripoli. Raymond III’s death shortly preceded the Battle of Hattin where Saladin decisively defeated the Crusader army. His legacy includes his long imprisonment his political maneuvering and his efforts to maintain stability in the Crusader states during a turbulent period.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.16611935198307037}, {"token": "Summary", "logprob": -0.8425891399383545}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0007640779949724674}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.15904387831687927}, {"token": " Wikipedia", "logprob": -8.77341881277971e-05}, {"token": " page", "logprob": -0.4741170406341553}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.143633171916008}, {"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0001494772732257843}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -2.7418097943154862e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -5.340433563105762e-05}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0036897454410791397}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -6.639736966462806e-05}, {"token": " Tripoli", "logprob": -1.5497195136049413e-06}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.0006666345288977027}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -5.4834770708112046e-05}, {"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.049650099128484726}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -3.790783375734463e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.18286018073558807}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.08142740279436111}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": " Tripoli", "logprob": -8.22540732769994e-06}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.000659248442389071}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.000846027978695929}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -1.0490362910786644e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00015341058315243572}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -0.0005999195855110884}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.00038771264371462166}, {"token": " until", "logprob": -1.137050747871399}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.02676062099635601}, {"token": " death", "logprob": -0.00022682955022901297}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.003282993333414197}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -